  "note": "Two parallel concrete box-girder decks carry four carriageways across the Vistula. Dark steel brackets support the widened wings and outside walking and cycling paths. Repeating paired columns, shallow profile, and a narrow median slot carry the silhouette. The viewer uses a 73 m sea-level datum and a shallow crest in the authored deck. Native terrain and water are retained. A 0.75 m bearing overlap at each end carries the replacement across adjoining PMTiles fragment endpoints. The mapped deck boundary scopes replacement of the crossing roads and paths. Ramps and lower routes remain native. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
